/**
 * eigen-web is a **static-assets-only Worker**: there is no `main`, so
 * Cloudflare's asset server answers every request and no Worker script is ever
 * invoked. (Workers with static assets is the current target for new projects;
 * Pages is only kept for existing ones.)
 *
 * Because there is no script, the C3 template's `nodejs_compat`,
 * `upload_source_maps` and `observability` keys were removed, since each of them
 * only configures a Worker script, and there isn't one.
 *
 * Deploys run in Workers Builds (repo-connected, production branch `main`,
 * non-production branch builds off), with root directory `web`, build command
 * `pnpm build`, and deploy command `pnpm exec wrangler deploy`. Workers Builds
 * must also define `PNPM_VERSION=11.20.0`: the pnpm 10 default cannot parse the
 * pnpm 11 multi-document lockfile. The deploy command must not use `npx`,
 * Cloudflare's default. npm enforces this package.json's
 * `devEngines.packageManager` (pnpm) and refuses to run at all, failing the
 * deploy step after a green build.
 *
 * `pnpm deploy` from a machine with `wrangler login` does the same thing.
 */
{
  "$schema": "node_modules/wrangler/config-schema.json",
  "name": "eigen-web",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-07-23",
  "assets": {
    "directory": "./build",
    // Docusaurus builds its own 404 page; serve that instead of a bare 404.
    "not_found_handling": "404-page"
  }
}
